<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gobelins Manufactory</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1662">1662</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gobelins Manufactory is a tapestry works in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, on the site of the dyeing workshops of the Gobelin family. In 1662 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert">Colbert</a> bought it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> and made it a royal manufactory producing tapestries and furniture for the royal palaces under the painter Charles Le Brun. It became a model of state-sponsored luxury industry and still operates under the French state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gobelins-manufactory.jpg" alt="Gobelins Manufactory" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manufacture_des_Gobelins.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
